# CLAUDE.md — resources (frontend)

<!-- if:islands -->
How the three frontend layers (Blade, htmx, Svelte islands) divide the work.
<!-- endif -->
<!-- unless:islands -->
How the two frontend layers (Blade and htmx) divide the work.
<!-- endif -->

## Layout

```
resources/
├── css/app.css                  # Tailwind 4 entry (+ htmx indicator rules)
├── js/
<!-- if:islands -->
│   ├── app.ts                   # htmx config (CSP, CSRF, 422) + islands boot
│   ├── islands.ts               # the registry: data-island → Svelte component
│   ├── islands/<Name>.svelte    # one file per island; filename = island name
<!-- endif -->
<!-- unless:islands -->
│   ├── app.ts                   # htmx config (CSP, CSRF, 422)
<!-- endif -->
│   ├── htmx-global.ts           # window.htmx, set before the extensions import
│   └── global.d.ts              # window.htmx typing
└── views/
    ├── components/layouts/app.blade.php   # <x-layouts.app :meta> (PageMeta)
<!-- if:islands -->
    ├── components/island.blade.php        # <x-island name :props>
<!-- endif -->
    ├── components/…                       # anonymous Blade components
    ├── partials/…                         # fragments shared by full page + htmx
    └── <feature>/…                        # pages, one directory per feature
```

A change not showing: the Vite dev server runs inside the local container (Hosting); `npm run build` makes the
production bundle.
<!-- if:islands -->
`npm run check` (svelte-check + tsc) is the type gate; it passes before any change under `resources/js` is done.
<!-- endif -->
<!-- unless:islands -->
`npm run check` (tsc) is the type gate; it passes before any change under `resources/js` is done.
<!-- endif -->

## Speed, SEO, smoothness

The practices behind root `CLAUDE.md`, Non-negotiables.

- **Complete without JS.** Every public page renders its full content server-side, with a real `<a href>` for every
  navigation. Nothing a crawler or a no-JS user needs sits behind `hx-get`, an island or a click. Tabs and accordions
  on public pages are CSS (`<details>`, `:target`) or server-rendered.
- **Head is per page, from the controller** (`PageMeta`, rendered by the layout; Blade below): title, description,
  canonical, Open Graph, JSON-LD from a Resource-shaped array, `hreflang` where a page exists in several locales. No
  public page leaves them empty.
- **Prefetch on public pages.** `hx-boost` + the htmx `preload` extension (`preload="mouseover"`, touchstart on
  mobile) on the main nav and listing links. A `speculationrules` block (CSP source `'inline-speculation-rules'`):
  `prefetch` for links in the viewport with moderate eagerness, `prerender` for the one most likely next page, picked
  by the controller. Never eager prefetch of whole listings, and never prefetch anything authenticated, with side
  effects, or not served by the response cache.
- **Zero layout shift.** Every `<img>` has `width`/`height` (or `aspect-ratio`), `loading="lazy"` below the fold,
  `srcset` + modern formats; the LCP image is eager with `fetchpriority="high"`. Placeholders are the size of what
  replaces them. Fonts are self-hosted woff2 from `resources/fonts/` (`@font-face` in `app.css`),
  `font-display: swap`, subset to the scripts we serve.
- **Smooth swaps.** No View Transitions (`globalViewTransitions = false`, never `transition:true`). `hx-indicator`
  only on requests that can be slow. `hx-sync` on filters, so typing does not queue requests. `hx-push-url` on
  boosted navigation; `hx-replace-url` for in-page state (filters, sort, view), so Back leaves the page.
<!-- if:islands -->
- **JavaScript on public pages** is `app.ts` plus the lazy chunks of that page's islands, loaded on first mount. An
  island mounts into a same-sized placeholder **after** the page is interactive, never on the critical path.
<!-- endif -->
<!-- unless:islands -->
- **JavaScript on public pages** is `app.ts` and nothing else.
<!-- endif -->
- **Secure-context APIs** (WebAuthn, `crypto.subtle`, `navigator.clipboard`) exist only on https or `localhost`
  (Hosting): code using one checks `window.isSecureContext` and says why the feature is unavailable, never throws.

## Who does what

| Need | Layer | Not |
|------|-------|-----|
<!-- if:islands -->
| Render a page, a list, a form | **Blade** | an island that fetches JSON |
| Submit, paginate, filter, reload part of a page | **htmx** (`hx-get`/`hx-post` → server renders the fragment) | `fetch()` in an island |
| Rich local state before/without a round trip (drag-drop, editors, pickers, live previews) | **Svelte island** | Blade + a pile of `hx-*` |
| Persist what an island did | a normal form submit / `htmx.ajax()` with the island's state in named hidden inputs (raw values) | an island-owned JSON API |
| Shared state between two islands on one page | a `resources/js/*.svelte.ts` module with runes | `window.*`, DOM attributes |

**htmx + Blade first.** If the htmx version is a couple of `hx-*` attributes and a fragment route, do that. An island
is justified only when local state changes many times before (or without) a round trip. If an island truly needs
JSON, its route lives in the page's `web` group (`api` is token-only) and returns a Resource, decided per case.
<!-- endif -->
<!-- unless:islands -->
| Render a page, a list, a form | **Blade** | JSON rendered by client code |
| Submit, paginate, filter, reload part of a page | **htmx** (`hx-get`/`hx-post` → server renders the fragment) | `fetch()` |
<!-- endif -->

## Blade

- Pages wrap in `<x-layouts.app :meta="$meta">` (`App\Services\Seo\PageMeta`; `:title` alone only for non-public
  pages). The layout owns `<head>`: title, description, canonical, robots, prev/next, OG, JSON-LD
  (`partials/seo/jsonld`, nonce, breadcrumbs included; never a second copy), the speculation rules
  (`PageMeta::speculationRules()`), the CSRF meta tag (only with a started session) and `@vite`. No page includes
  assets itself. `hx-boost` goes per navigation block, never on `<body>`.
- **Full page and fragment are the same markup.** `@include` a partial from both the page and the fragment route, or
  wrap the section in `@fragment('name')` and return `view(…)->fragment('name')`. Fragment ids are the read-path
  contract: stable names, one per page.
- Anonymous components (`resources/views/components/*.blade.php`) for presentational reuse; a class-based one only
  when it needs PHP. A leaf rendered per row (money, icon, image, chip, date) is a plain partial, not an `<x-*>`
  (~0.1 ms per component render adds up across a listing).
<!-- if:islands -->
- `{{ }}` always. `{!! !!}` only for `Markdown::render()` output, the layout's inlined stylesheet (`Vite::content`, a
  compiled asset) and `$user->twoFactorQrCodeSvg()`. Never `@json($model)`: client data goes through
  `<x-island :props>` or a Resource.
<!-- endif -->
<!-- unless:islands -->
- `{{ }}` always. `{!! !!}` only for `Markdown::render()` output, the layout's inlined stylesheet (`Vite::content`, a
  compiled asset) and `$user->twoFactorQrCodeSvg()`. Never `@json($model)`: client data goes through a Resource.
<!-- endif -->
- Enum display is `$model->status->label()` (`app/Enums/CLAUDE.md`), never a `@switch` on `->value`.
- Named routes everywhere: `route()` in `href`, `action` and every `hx-*` URL.
- **Cached pages ship stateless markup.** A plain cookie mirrors what the page shows (a count, a badge), read by
  `app.ts` on load and after every swap. `@csrf` renders only with a started session, never into shared cached HTML.
- Overlays are native HTML (`<dialog>`, the Popover API, `<details>`), opened and closed by delegated listeners in
  `app.ts`; tabs are real links. Toasts come from an `HX-Trigger` header the layout's listener renders.
- Icons come from one sprite the layout renders once; views `<use>` it, never inline SVG paths. A standalone icon gets
  a label.
- Form controls wire `aria-invalid` and `aria-describedby` to their hint and error ids; errors come from `$errors`.
- **Blade gotchas.** Text right after a closing slot tag on the same line (`</x-slot:header>Body`) compiles to
  `@endslotBody`, which leaks into the page: break the line. A directive glued to a word (`word@if`) is not compiled,
  and one glued to a component's closing tag (`/>@endif`) breaks the compile: leave a space, and put the branch's own
  space inside the branch.

## htmx

Configured once in `app.ts`, never per element:

- `allowEval = false` (CSP) → **no `hx-on:*`, no `hx-vals='js:…'`, no `hx-trigger` filters (`click[cond]` is
  evaluated).**
<!-- if:islands -->
  Behaviour that needs JS is an island or a listener in `app.ts`.
<!-- endif -->
<!-- unless:islands -->
  Behaviour that needs JS is a listener in `app.ts`.
<!-- endif -->
- `selfRequestsOnly = true`: htmx only talks to this origin.
- The CSRF header is added once in `htmx:configRequest`; **no per-form `hx-headers`**.
- 422 responses are swapped (`htmx:beforeSwap`): a failed FormRequest re-renders the form fragment with `$errors`.
- `includeIndicatorStyles = false`: the `.htmx-indicator` rules live in `app.css`.
- After a successful htmx POST, redirect with `HX-Redirect`, never a 302 (htmx would swap the whole page into the
  target).
- Flash messages for htmx callers come back **in the fragment** (or a toast via `HX-Trigger`), never
  `back()->with()`.
<!-- if:tenancy -->
- **The tenant marker** (root `CLAUDE.md`, Tenancy): the authenticated layout renders
  `<meta name="tenant" content="<current tenant id>">`. The project adds to `app.ts`: `htmx:configRequest` sends it as
  `X-Tenant` beside the CSRF header, and `htmx:beforeSwap` answers a 409 `tenant_changed` with the message and a full
  reload. A form that can post without htmx carries a hidden `_tenant`. The switcher is a form posting `tenant` to
  `route('current-tenant.update')`.
<!-- endif -->

## Auth pages

<!-- unless:auth-pages -->
Fortify's views stay off, with `AcceptJson`, until the project builds these pages ("Build the auth pages" is an open
item):
<!-- endif -->
<!-- if:auth-pages -->
Fortify's views are on and serve these pages:
<!-- endif -->
`resources/views/auth/<name>`, the names `Fortify::viewPrefix('auth.')` registers, built from the project's
components inside the app layout, `noindex`:

- `login`: email, password, remember, "Forgot password", a passkey button plus autofill
  (`autocomplete="email webauthn"`), the status and social errors; once social sign-in is built, one button per
  enabled provider → `route('social.redirect', …)`.
- `register` (registration on): name, email, password + confirmation; provider buttons once social sign-in is built.
- `forgot-password`: email → status.
- `reset-password`: hidden token, email, password + confirmation.
- `two-factor-challenge`: code or recovery code; no JS.
- `confirm-password`: password and "Confirm with a passkey"; a user with neither gets the "sign out and use Forgot
  password" line (root `CLAUDE.md`, Auth).
- `verify-email` (email verification on): resend → `verification.send`.

Around them:
- Each is a plain `<form method="post" action="{{ route(…) }}">` with `@csrf` and `hx-boost="false"`: sign-in,
  sign-out and registration regenerate the CSRF token, and a boosted swap would keep the old one in the head meta.
- Passkeys: `@laravel/passkeys` (convention 6) in `resources/js/passkeys.ts`, bound from `app.ts` by
  delegated listeners on `data-passkey-*` attributes (CSP). It sends `Accept: application/json` and the `csrf-token`
  meta, and on success navigates to the returned `redirect`.
- A security settings page behind `auth` + `password.confirm`: two-factor enable/confirm/disable with the QR code and
  recovery codes, passkeys add/remove, linked providers, password; only for the features kept. Its forms are plain
  too: an unconfirmed action gets a 302 to the confirm page, which htmx would swap into the target.

<!-- unless:auth-pages -->
**The views flip** lands in the commit that adds the last page:
- `Fortify::viewPrefix('auth.')` in `FortifyServiceProvider`, `'views' => true` in `config/fortify.php`, and a
  `fortify.home` that names a page that exists;
- drop `AcceptJson` (from `fortify.middleware`, the priority list in `bootstrap/app.php` and `app/Http/Middleware/`)
  and the `ResetPassword::createUrlUsing` override (`password.reset` now exists);
- rewrite `tests/E2E/FortifyViewRoutesTest.php` for views on: the GET pages answer 200 instead of 405, a guest on an
  authenticated auth route is redirected to `login`, and the JSON flows send `Accept: application/json` (`postJson`,
  `getJson`);
- add `auth-pages` to `modules` in `config/house.php` and run `php artisan house:update`, then
  `php artisan boost:update`: the house rules turn to views on (root `CLAUDE.md`, Auth; `routes/`, `app/Http/`,
  `app/Providers/` and this file).
<!-- endif -->

<!-- if:islands -->
## Svelte islands

- **One file per island** in `resources/js/islands/`, PascalCase, `<script lang="ts">`, Svelte 5 runes (`$props`,
  `$state`, `$derived`); no legacy `export let` or stores as state.
- Registered automatically by filename. `islands.ts` globs the directory **lazily**: an island's code downloads on
  first mount, so unused islands cost a page nothing. Mounted from Blade:

  ```blade
  <x-island name="TaskBoard" :props="TaskBoardResource::make($board)->resolve()">
      <span class="text-sm text-muted">Loading…</span>   {{-- placeholder --}}
  </x-island>
  ```

  `:props` is JSON-safe data from a Resource (or a plain array of scalars), **never a model**: the Resource is the
  leak boundary, and Blade's escaping of the attribute keeps user text from breaking out.
- Props are typed: `let { start = 0 }: { start?: number } = $props();`. Everything the island needs arrives as props;
  it never reads the DOM outside its own element, or `window` globals.
- **Lifecycle is handled.** `app.ts` mounts islands on page load and every `htmx:load`, and unmounts on
  `htmx:beforeCleanupElement`. An island in a swapped fragment remounts with fresh props: state that must survive a
  swap is the server's.
- Tailwind classes work inside islands (no shadow DOM). `<style>` blocks only for what utilities cannot express.
- `{@html}` follows the `{!! !!}` rule: `Markdown::render()` output only.
- No fetching inside islands by default (Who does what). An island that does fetch renders a failed load as an error
  state: what failed, the server's message (a 429 says when to retry) and a retry action, never nothing. No global
  event bus; shared state is an explicit `*.svelte.ts` module.
- `npm run check` is clean. Suppress a Svelte warning only with a `svelte-ignore` comment that says why.

## Components: shadcn-svelte

The first island that needs a component does the setup, with these devDependencies (convention 6): `shadcn-svelte`
(exact pin), `bits-ui`, `tailwind-variants`, `cn` (at the range the pinned registry's `utils` item declares),
`tw-animate-css`, `@lucide/svelte`.

- **No `init`**: it calls a live endpoint that cannot be pinned, injects a font and re-pins `shadcn-svelte@latest`.
  Its outputs are project files, written once:
  - `components.json` at the root: `style` set explicitly (an unknown style silently becomes another),
    `typescript: true`, `tailwind.css` = `resources/css/shadcn.css`, aliases `@/components`, `@/components/ui`,
    `@/lib/utils`, `@/hooks`, `@/lib`, and `registry` =
    `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/huntabyte/shadcn-svelte/shadcn-svelte@<version>/docs/static/registry`, where
    `<version>` is the exact `shadcn-svelte` devDependency;
  - `resources/js/lib/utils.ts`: the registry's `utils` item as the pinned CLI writes it (`cn` re-exported from the
    `cn` package, plus the types `WithElementRef`, `WithoutChild`, `WithoutChildren` and `WithoutChildrenOrChild`);
  - the `check:ui` script.
- `@` is `resources/js`: laravel-vite-plugin aliases it, and the shipped `tsconfig.json` `paths` cover it (the CLI
  reads `paths` from the root tsconfig only).
- **Add** with the pinned CLI (`npx shadcn-svelte@<version> add <name> --no-deps-install`), only what an island
  imports; remove a component no island uses. No `sonner`: toasts come from `HX-Trigger`. Then `git diff package.json`: a new entry is a package the component declares, approved with
  shadcn-svelte, so `npm install` it; a changed range on an existing entry goes back to the project's. Review the
  rest of its diff as code.
- `resources/js/components/ui/` is exactly the CLI's output and is never edited. Looks go through the `class` prop
  (`cn` merges it last), variants through `tv({ extend: buttonVariants, … })` in `resources/js/components/<area>/`,
  behaviour through a wrapper component there.
- **Update**: bump the `shadcn-svelte` pin, the registry tag and `cn`'s range (the new `utils` item's) together,
  rerun `add <every installed component> --yes --overwrite`, commit `ui/` as generated. Generated code that fails
  `npm run check` means another pin (the newest that passes), never an edit.
- **The gate is `npm run check:ui`.** In a temp dir holding a minimal `package.json`, the same tsconfig `paths`,
  `components.json` and the same CSS files, it runs the pinned CLI with
  `add <every directory in ui/> --yes --overwrite --no-deps-install` and fails on any diff in `ui/`. It needs the
  registry host, so it is not part of `npm run check`; it runs before a push that touches `ui/`, `components.json` or
  the pin.
- **CSS**: `resources/css/app.css` is the one Tailwind entry. It imports, in this order, `tailwindcss`,
  `tw-animate-css`, `shadcn-svelte/tailwind.css`, `./shadcn.css` and `./theme.css`, then holds the house `@theme`.
  - `shadcn.css` is CLI-managed: no `@import "tailwindcss"`, only its `@theme inline`, `:root`/`.dark` and a
    hand-declared `@custom-variant dark (&:is(.dark *))`.
  - `theme.css` maps `--primary`, `--radius`, … in `:root` and `.dark` onto the house tokens. The CLI never touches
    it and it comes last, so an `add` that overwrites `:root` values in `shadcn.css` changes nothing visible. House
    tokens never use shadcn's names (no `--color-primary`, `--color-background`, …).
- Forms in islands use the `field` component, not `form`, which imports `$app/*` modules an island does not have.
  `Field.Error` takes `{ message }[]`: `errors={msgs.map((message) => ({ message }))}`.
- Icons inside islands come from `@lucide/svelte`.

<!-- endif -->
## Tailwind

- Tailwind 4, config-less: the design tokens (colour, type, spacing, grid) live only in `@theme` in `app.css`.
- **Semantic colour means something**: one token per meaning, never decoration, never colour alone.
- A view is components, partials and utilities over those tokens: no hex, font family, one-off spacing or
  page-specific stylesheet. A pattern needed twice becomes a component first.
- Money, numbers and time are formatted in exactly one place each (a partial or a `Support` formatter). Never
  concatenate a price, a number or a date in Blade.
- Breakpoint gotcha: Tailwind emits arbitrary `min-[…]:` variants *before* the named ones, so
  `xl:w-64 min-[1440px]:w-80` resolves to `w-64`. Use a base class plus the arbitrary override, never both variants on
  one property.
<!-- if:islands -->
- Blade and `.svelte` files under `resources/` are scanned automatically; vendor Blade that needs scanning is listed
  with `@source` in `app.css`.
<!-- endif -->
<!-- unless:islands -->
- Blade files under `resources/` are scanned automatically; vendor Blade that needs scanning is listed with `@source`
  in `app.css`.
<!-- endif -->

## Tests

A page or fragment flow is an E2E test through `$this->get(route(…))`, with `HX-Request` for a fragment
(`tests/CLAUDE.md`).
<!-- house:end -->
